  "comments": [
    {"at":0,"placement":"line","text":"Animates both fighters and draws them into the work bitmap. The drawing order sets which fighter is in front. When fighter 1 does one of the 4 moves at $bd79, fighter 0 goes first. During set-up ($ba bit 7) it does nothing. When $bb bit 7 is set, it animates only fighter 0."},
    {"at":41,"placement":"line","text":"Steps the move sequence of fighter X by one byte and draws the new pose. The sequence of move $67,x comes from the pointers at $bc87. A byte below $ff is a pose number. $ff is a command. The next byte: 0 = start again, 1 = stop, 2 = go to an index. Command 3 starts the next move. A higher command holds the last pose. At move $9d (turn), command 3 also changes the facing and moves the fighter by $7f4a."},
    {"at":57,"placement":"side","text":"7 pairs of move and frame at $c885/$c88c start the sound at $c893."},
    {"at":99,"placement":"side","text":"The last pose of the sequence: the move can be interrupted."},
    {"at":107,"placement":"side","text":"The pose number selects a pose record at $bd80."},
    {"at":168,"placement":"side","text":"Move $9d is the turn: it changes the facing."},
    {"at":180,"placement":"side","text":"The new facing clears bit 7 of $b2."},
    {"at":201,"placement":"side","text":"Fighter 1 turned: requests the mirror of the shared sprites."},
    {"at":221,"placement":"side","text":"Shows the last pose again."}
  ],
